        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "To enable error handling for a V2G communication session setup the EVCC monitors the time between reception of SECC discovery response, SessionSetupRes and PowerDeliveryRes, respectively. This allows the EVCC to decide about a successful or failed charging session after the defined timeouts.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                168,
                1053,
                247
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    168.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    168.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    247.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    247.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The monitoring of a V2G communication session is based on the following timing concepts:",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                269,
                931,
                296
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    269.0
                ],
                [
                    931.0,
                    269.0
                ],
                [
                    931.0,
                    296.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    296.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "– message timing: monitors the timing between the request and the response of a Request-Response-Pair. This allows, for example, the EVCC application to initiate the error handling if no response is sent;",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                302,
                1052,
                380
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    302.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    302.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    380.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    380.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "– sequence timing: monitors the timing of subsequent request-response-pairs. This allows, for example, the SECC application to initiate the error handling if an expected next request message was not sent;",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                385,
                1052,
                462
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    385.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    385.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    462.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    462.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- ongoing timing: monitors the timing in case of sending a request-response-pair repeatedly based on the parameter EVSEProcessing equal to \"Ongoing\". This allows, for example, the EVCC to initiate the error handling in case the SECC exceeds the processing time;",
            "block_bbox": [
                102,
                469,
                1052,
                546
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    102.0,
                    469.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    469.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    546.0
                ],
                [
                    102.0,
                    546.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- communication setup timing: monitors the time from the moment of an established data link until the session setup message. It allows deciding if the communication setup was successful within a defined time.",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                552,
                1054,
                629
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    552.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    552.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    629.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    629.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The timers are compared to predefined time values as decision criterion. The EVCC and the SECC distinguish between two categories:",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                653,
                1053,
                705
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    653.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    653.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    705.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    705.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- timeout: if the specified time is exceeded the related error handling is initiated:",
            "block_bbox": [
                102,
                711,
                891,
                737
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    101.85540008544922,
                    717.0010986328125
                ],
                [
                    890.0,
                    711.0
                ],
                [
                    890.1446533203125,
                    729.9989013671875
                ],
                [
                    102.00006103515625,
                    736.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- performance time: if the specified time is exceeded the performance requirement is not fulfilled.",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                743,
                1048,
                770
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
